WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.042
Right, then. I've got a bath running
so I'm gonna make this quick.

00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:04.500
This is everything
you need to know

00:00:04.583 --> 00:00:06.042
about season one of The Witcher.

00:00:06.292 --> 00:00:07.542
Welcome to the Continent,

00:00:07.625 --> 00:00:11.459
a land of prophecies, monsters,
mages, elves, and witchers.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.583
A witcher is basically
a monster hunter.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.639
There are few left in this world.
This one is called…

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:16.589
Geralt of Rivia.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.792
So, one day, Geralt comes across
these two, Stregobor and Renfri,

00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:22.625
who want to kill each other,
but believe Geralt, the monster hunter,

00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:24.000
can do the deed for them.

00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:25.214
-They think it's…
-Destiny.

00:00:25.307 --> 00:00:28.332
And Geralt's like, "Nobody tells me
what to do, not even destiny."

00:00:28.585 --> 00:00:30.667
But then he does get involved
to protect the innocent

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.042
and kills Renfri,
who in her last breath mutters…

00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:35.603
The girl in the woods
is your destiny.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.333
He's like,
"There's that word again."

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:39.788
And then these ungrateful clowns
cast him out of town.

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:42.298
A bard called Jaskier joins Geralt
on his quest, and is like…

00:00:42.373 --> 00:00:43.875
You have got an image problem.

00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:45.853
I could change
the public's tune about you.

00:00:45.993 --> 00:00:47.667
Geralt gets his ass kicked
by a goat man

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.151
and they are captured by elves.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.917
King of the elves,
Filavandrel, is like…

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.167
My elders worked with humans.
They were slaughtered.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.750
He goes to cut Geralt's throat,
who's like, "Whatever, mate. Just…"

00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:57.714
Don't call me human.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.722
So the elves let them go,
after which this song,

00:00:59.806 --> 00:01:01.579
that never lets you sleep,
was born.

00:01:01.654 --> 00:01:02.542
You know the words.

00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:05.000
Toss a coin to your witcher…

00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:06.708
Jaskier's like, "I did you a favor,

00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:08.500
so in return,
you can bodyguard me in Cintra,

00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:10.417
the most powerful land
on the Continent."

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.042
Queen Calanthe
is deciding on a suitor

00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:14.083
to marry her daughter,
Princess Pavetta.

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.625
At this point, the kingdom
of Nilfgaard is known to be

00:01:16.708 --> 00:01:18.875
the less powerful shithole city
further south.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.471
More on them jokers later.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.833
No!

00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:25.417
Suddenly, a cursed porcupine man
called Duny is all like,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.333
"I have the right
to your daughter's hand in marriage."

00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:29.125
By the Law of Surprise.

00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:30.667
For anyone pretending they know
what that means…

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.375
Slay this beast!

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:35.375
…if you save someone from a certain death
and don't want money,

00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:37.469
you can claim payment
with the Law of Surprise.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.292
Destiny then determines
that payment,

00:01:39.375 --> 00:01:41.500
which is something the other person
already possesses

00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:42.625
but doesn't know about.

00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:43.917
Make sense?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.981
-Well…
-Good.

00:01:45.542 --> 00:01:48.167
Of course, Geralt saves Duny
from certain death,

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.083
these guys get married,
and the curse is lifted.

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.958
As payment for saving his life,
Geralt thinks, "I'll give this a whirl,"

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.375
-and claims…
-The Law of Surprise.

00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:56.125
It turns out Pavetta is pregnant,

00:01:56.208 --> 00:01:58.167
and Geralt's ecstatic
when he realizes

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.208
-that the baby is for him to claim.
-Fuck.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.583
This wizard man's like,
"Destiny has spoken."

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:05.333
"If you leave without claiming
this child, we're all fucked."

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:06.750
-And Geralt's like…
-Bullshit.

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:08.250
"Nobody tells me what to do."

00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:10.500
But after some years
of not being able to sleep,

00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:12.222
Geralt finds a djinn
to fix his problem.

00:02:12.309 --> 00:02:13.373
Not that kind of gin.

00:02:13.448 --> 00:02:15.511
It's more like a genie… in a bottle.

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:17.190
This one attacks Jaskier,

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.083
and Geralt finds help
from this saucy mage.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.375
Yennefer of Vengerberg.

00:02:20.458 --> 00:02:23.167
Who is Yennefer of Vengerberg?
Let's go back and find out.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.500
Born with a twisted spine,

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:26.833
Yennefer was bought
by a sorceress named Tissaia

00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:28.792
and taken to Aretuza,
a school of magic,

00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:31.250
where they learn how to use
this thing called Chaos,

00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:33.583
which is basically a magical force
that mages harness

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.792
to move stuff and…
Well, you get the gist.

00:02:36.707 --> 00:02:39.708
Yennefer's BF or FB, Istredd,
is spying on her,

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.674
-and tells the Brotherhood…
-She's part elf.

00:02:41.833 --> 00:02:42.792
Everyone hates elves,

00:02:42.875 --> 00:02:45.333
so they vote to send Yennefer
to the shitty city Nilfgaard.

00:02:45.417 --> 00:02:46.619
Instead of Fringilla.

00:02:46.706 --> 00:02:50.311
But Yennefer's like, "Fuck that.
Make me powerful… and pretty."

00:02:50.486 --> 00:02:52.250
This guy's like, "You won't
be able to have children."

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:55.458
And she's thinking, "That sounds fixable."
He's thinking, "It's not."

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.187
And boom,
sexy Yennefer swoops in

00:02:57.281 --> 00:02:59.583
and wins over a king
far away from Nilfgaard.

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:01.664
Someone has to go there.
Fringilla, you up for it?

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:02.625
Never mind.

00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:04.583
Since then, Yennefer has been
roaming the land

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.875
to find a cure for her womb,
so when Geralt says…

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:08.292
He was attacked by a djinn.

00:03:08.375 --> 00:03:10.167
She's like, "Bingo! Baby."

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.963
But it gets out of control and
Geralt makes a wish to save her.

00:03:13.048 --> 00:03:14.975
The djinn's like,
"I'm free! I'm finally free!"

00:03:15.198 --> 00:03:18.072
Yennefer's pissed off, but is like,
"Let's just check to see if it worked."

00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:19.083
She wakes up,

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.856
and commitment-phobe Geralt
has ghosted her, that bastard.

00:03:21.953 --> 00:03:23.811
-Don't judge me.
-Okay, fair enough.

00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:25.833
Sometime later,
they coincidentally

00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:27.750
enter the same race
to hunt down a dragon.

00:03:27.829 --> 00:03:29.504
-Geralt's like…
-What are you doing here, Yen?

00:03:29.579 --> 00:03:31.708
And she's like, "Duh!
Dragon hearts cure wombs."

00:03:31.958 --> 00:03:34.748
We find out that Nilfgaard has
returned, burning through the south.

00:03:34.925 --> 00:03:36.208
With Fringilla as their mage.

00:03:36.375 --> 00:03:38.292
You remember Fringilla,
Yennefer's mate from school?

00:03:38.375 --> 00:03:41.283
Well this is her new mate, Cahir,
Nilfgaard's commanding officer.

00:03:41.562 --> 00:03:42.417
He's cool.

00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:44.147
Meanwhile, Geralt lets this slip…

00:03:44.247 --> 00:03:46.764
I'd rather use my Child Surprise
as bruxa bait!

00:03:46.851 --> 00:03:48.167
You have a Child Surprise?

00:03:48.292 --> 00:03:50.375
Busted.
But what the hell is a bruxa?

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.417
Well, it's basically a… Wait.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.458
It's definitely too soon to say that.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.081
But if you watch season two,
you can find out for yourself.

00:03:57.233 --> 00:03:58.258
Back to these lovebirds.

00:03:58.333 --> 00:04:01.000
Knowing Geralt's abandoned a child
when Yennefer is desperate for one

00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:02.375
is a bitter pill to swallow.

00:04:02.625 --> 00:04:04.250
-Fuck.
-Well recovered, Geralt.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:07.708
After much drama, action,
and some sweaty sex for good measure,

00:04:07.792 --> 00:04:10.125
Yennefer realizes that
Geralt made a wish with the djinn.

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:11.958
That's why we can't escape each other.

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:13.875
She's like, "It's not love, it's magic."

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.083
Yennefer dumps Geralt,

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:17.375
-and Geralt tells Jaskier to do one.
-Right, then.

00:04:17.525 --> 00:04:20.062
Geralt sees the now-enormous
army of Nilfgaard, and thinks…

00:04:20.909 --> 00:04:23.167
"Maybe I should go to Cintra
and check on that kid,"

00:04:23.321 --> 00:04:25.875
who is now Princess Cirilla,
or Ciri, of Cintra.

00:04:26.042 --> 00:04:27.375
She's been raised
by her grandparents

00:04:27.458 --> 00:04:29.297
after her actual parents were lost at sea.

00:04:29.392 --> 00:04:32.500
-Geralt gets to Cintra and is like…
-I'm here to protect the girl.

00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:33.875
But then Calanthe is like…

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.375
You and destiny
can both fuck right off.

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:38.188
And locks him in the dungeon.

00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:40.083
Nilfgaard attack,
kill the king,

00:04:41.276 --> 00:04:42.397
and take over the city.

00:04:42.612 --> 00:04:45.542
Meanwhile the Brotherhood of Mages hear
of Nilfgaard attacking Cintra.

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:47.292
-What?
-And jump at the chance to help.

00:04:47.435 --> 00:04:48.331
Who cares?

00:04:48.481 --> 00:04:52.292
Okay, so only a small group of mages
team up to stop Nilfgaard at Sodden Hill.

00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:53.991
Hold Sodden, save the Continent.

00:04:54.066 --> 00:04:55.917
Back in Cintra, Calanthe,
on her deathbed, is like,

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.542
-"Maybe Geralt can help."
-Geralt!

00:04:57.708 --> 00:04:59.736
Of course, he's fucked off
to release his frustrations.

00:04:59.958 --> 00:05:01.750
In her last breath, she tells Ciri…

00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:03.875
Find Geralt of Rivia.

00:05:03.958 --> 00:05:05.292
He is your destiny.

00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:06.958
And Ciri's like, "Geralt of what?"

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.631
She leaves with this hero,

00:05:09.076 --> 00:05:10.208
is captured by Cahir,

00:05:10.292 --> 00:05:13.083
but, luckily, discovers she has
these mega screaming powers…

00:05:14.625 --> 00:05:17.167
which you could argue
are groundbreaking.

00:05:17.292 --> 00:05:19.625
Ciri escapes into the woods
and Cahir is left thinking,

00:05:19.708 --> 00:05:22.750
"How the hell am I gonna
explain this to my boss?"

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:24.625
After some days on the run,

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.042
-Ciri meets this elf.
-I'm Dara.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.750
They escape Nilfgaard and Cahir
again at a refugee camp,

00:05:28.958 --> 00:05:30.499
arrive at an enchanted forest,

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.616
Ciri has a trippy dream,
and they bump into this weirdo.

00:05:34.409 --> 00:05:37.259
To which Dara's like, "Screw you,
Bad Luck Princess. I'm off."

00:05:38.083 --> 00:05:40.083
Ciri goes at it alone
and is once again attacked,

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.042
but after reciting
some badass poetry…

00:05:42.125 --> 00:05:45.125
The Time of Madness
and the Time of Contempt.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.333
…we cut to black.

00:05:46.417 --> 00:05:48.625
Geralt arrives at the refugee camp
looking for Ciri,

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:50.292
gets bitten by
this lanky motherfucker,

00:05:50.375 --> 00:05:51.779
and wakes up tripping his balls off.

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:53.917
Turns out this guy saved him
and they're off to get help.

00:05:54.458 --> 00:05:57.000
Ciri wakes up and realizes
she's exploded or something,

00:05:57.125 --> 00:05:58.333
killing all these assholes.

00:05:58.417 --> 00:06:00.708
She goes with this woman,
who lives near the Battle of Sodden.

00:06:00.792 --> 00:06:03.917
Where Nilfgaard are like, "Nobody calls me
a joker. Who's laughing now?"

00:06:04.042 --> 00:06:07.167
And Yennefer's like, "Me," and burns
the shit out of them, saving the day.

00:06:07.248 --> 00:06:08.750
Fire magic is illegal, by the way.

00:06:08.833 --> 00:06:11.251
Ciri has a weird dream of Geralt
and Tissaia looking for Yennefer,

00:06:11.326 --> 00:06:13.186
wakes up, and goes
for a stroll in the woods.

00:06:13.304 --> 00:06:16.000
In that moment, Geralt arrives
at the same house Ciri was just at,

00:06:16.125 --> 00:06:18.945
goes into the woods,
and is finally met with Ciri.

00:06:19.095 --> 00:06:20.401
Destiny prevails.

00:06:20.771 --> 00:06:22.083
-Ciri's like…
-Who is Yennefer?

00:06:22.338 --> 00:06:23.667
And Geralt's like, "What the fuck?"

00:06:23.958 --> 00:06:25.125
Right, that's your lot.

00:06:25.208 --> 00:06:27.167
You should be all prepped now
for season two.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:28.542
You are welcome.

